{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1435137-new-immortal-the-hucksters","id":1435137,"title":"New Immortal, the hucksters.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-10T18:25:01-08:00","id":1435137,"title":"New Immortal, the hucksters.","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">New Immortal</span></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, </span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Hucksters </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">A long time ago there was a gambler who was afraid of dying and in doing so he went into the occult and discovered a method when he met a being called the lord of chance. They played a game with the gambler\u2019s soul as the wager, the gambler won and the lord gave him a secret method on which years of someone\u2019s life could be bet. Any game of chance or skill could be used. But it had to be fair, both parties had to know what they were getting into and the bet had to be even, although another could wager based on a proxy as long as both parties agreed to it. Each huckster has a favored game, some choose games of pure skill, because they are that good at it. Others choose games of luck provided by skill to make things more fair or because they are not that good. Some choose obscure games so they often come up against beginners others choose common games played for two. Some choose to stay young which allows them more access to ignorant kids who are more willing to bet ridiculous things on games of chance and skill. So they often go for children\u2019s games, collectible card games are popular ones. Some choose to stay old so they are willing to find people who fear death and are more likely to agree to the wager. Some bet small sums of their lifespan on the games which is safer but leaves a trail of losses that can track them down later, immortality doesn\u2019t protect against a 9mm. Some only play rarely and bet large numbers of years on a game, which lets the trail go cold but if they lose they lose big time. The effects on the huckster in question vary according to the deal and the method of the wager, some de age and age normally, others stop aging at a certain point until their years are used up, some de-age to a desired age and only age after the excess years are used up. The efficiency of the deal can vary. Some have a 1 to 1 year ratio of time lived vs aging, others are not so lucky. The dice pool is Resolve + Presence after losing a game of chance for whatever dice pool that is. If you succeed the bargain is struck.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Huckster Merits: </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Slow Leak 1-5: Your character has managed to slow her aging. However much you age divide the amount of time by the amount of merit dots you have. For example a character with 5 dots in this merit would only age 1 year every 5 years.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Game master 1-5: Most hucksters only have only managed to complete the deal with only one game type. With this merit you can use another game for the deal at one merit dot. 3 Games for two merit dots. Five games total for 3 merit dots. 7 games for 4 merit dots and 13 games for 5 merit dots.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Spendthrift 1-5: You can spend years that you have to alleviate damage, 10 years per dot of bashing damage, 30 years per dot of lethal damage 50 years per dot of aggravated damage. Each merit dot allows an additional point of damage per turn to be healed in this manner with an instant action.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Forever young: 1-5 You can spend years to turn back your biological clock instead of just stopping it with a 1-1 ratio. With each merit dot you gain an extra ten years back from the age you are currently.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prime time: 3 When you strike the bargain you can maintain the same age constantly as long as you have years to live but when you run out of years you age to your chronological age which might end up killing you.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ace up your sleeve: 1-5 You can spend years, to enhance your social or physical or mental attributes. For ten years a dot for one scene. The limit is defined by the amount of merit dots you have in this merit. You have to buy this merit again if you want to enhance another set of attributes.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> I had this for a while, but I thought it could fit in with that minor guild of oracles and gamblers, just a thought.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26513-laguz-24","name":"Laguz 24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26513_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T02:03:47-08:00","id":1437211,"title":"","content":"Your idea probably isn't going to stand out with that &quot;minor guild of oracles and gamblers&quot; in the mind of the fandom. Give them something distinctive from that guild or they will fade into obscurity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T07:58:34-08:00","id":1437232,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I came up with them before mummy came out. So, yeah, it's kind of a bummer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26513-laguz-24","name":"Laguz 24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26513_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}